      ":question/worked-solution": "Let's plot the graph of $y=\\tan x.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/generate/scratch/17592186176049/tangent.png)\n\nLet's go through each statement.\n\n- Statement I is false. The zeros occur at $x=0,\\pm\\pi,\\pm2\\pi,\\ldots,$ which can be written as $x=n\\pi.$\n\n- Statement II is true. The function has an asymptote at $x=\\frac{\\pi}{2}$ and the period is $\\pi.$ Therefore, the asymptotes occur at $x=\\frac{\\pi}{2}+n\\pi.$\n\n- Statement III is false. The function takes values on all the real numbers, hence the range is $(-\\infty,\\infty).$\n\nSo, the correct answer is \"II only\"."
